//! Captured packets used as the skeleton for the ones we emit.
//!
//! # Why a template and not a constructor
//!
//! A CDJ status packet is 284 bytes of which about a dozen can be named and
//! roughly 260 cannot. Across 749 consecutive packets from an idle
//! CDJ-2000nexus only **six** bytes ever changed: the USB slot state, the
//! link-available flag, two still-unidentified bytes at `0x6a` and `0x74`, and
//! the packet counter (F23).
//!
//! Building one field by field would therefore mean inventing values for 260
//! bytes we do not understand, and sending a plausible zero has broken playback
//! twice (F33, F35). Starting from a real packet and substituting only the
//! fields we understand is the difference between plausible and
//! indistinguishable.
//!
//! Both templates were captured from the author's own hardware — a CDJ-2000NXS
//! on firmware 1.44 — with the identifying and per-medium fields zeroed, so
//! nothing about the source deck is baked in.

